/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1648), [interaction.ts:1729](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1729), [interaction.ts:1768](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1768) | [“a stream commit that moves the bands…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-hold.browser.test.ts:187) derives the expected band from the fixture and rule 3b. **None** exercises eviction of the held datum itself. |\n    17\t| 11 · Cached AX160 and reader note | Major | **Fixed** | Tick failures are cached with the axis parts and republished when the ready layout returns. [axes.ts:85](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:85), [controller.ts:1250](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1250) | [“a throwing y tick formatter: AX160 and the note survive…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:156). §3.5 and F12. |\n    18\t| 12 · Mutable dates and zoom round-trip | Major | **Fixed** | Options and zoom snapshot `Date` inputs. Fractional positions are emitted as numbers. [options.ts:44](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/options.ts:44), [controller.ts:195](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:195), [controller.ts:817](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:817) | [“a Date in x.domain mutated and resubmitted…”, “a Date passed to zoom()…”, and “a window between milliseconds…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:175). Fixture timestamps and the public round-trip contract. |\n    19\t| 13 · Compact zoom and secondary tick formats | Major | **Fixed** | Compact zoom exits before accepting a window. The resolver reports AX150 for every unused compact tick formatter. [controller.ts:807](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:807), [data/options.ts:239](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/options.ts:239) | [“no event, AX150, and nothing applied when compact is turned off”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:216) and [“compact %s: x and every y field”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/diagnostics/registry.test.ts:266). §3.7 and F3. |\n    20\t| 14 · Watcher cleanup and reattachment | Major | **Partly fixed** | Theme setup rolls back and successful reattachment clears font measurements. A failure during reattachment can still leave prior subscriptions live and `watching` set. [watch.ts:34](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/watch.ts:34), [chart.ts:91](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:91), [chart.ts:148](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:148) | [“the theme observer’s observe() throws…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:235) catches a full revert under DX5. Its shared `Set` counts the same callback once across three targets. **None** checks font widths after reattachment or rollback of the full watcher sequence. |\n    21\t| 15 · Automatic numeric x endpoints | Major | **Partly fixed** | The original line domain is correct under amended F7. Ordinary scatter uses endpoint tick candidates, but the candidate extent excludes missing-y positions and the layout can drop an endpoint. [spec F7](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:100), [view/index.ts:220](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:220), [axes.ts:137](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:137) | [“a line on x 1.1 to 8.9…” and “a scatter on x 1.1 to 8.9…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:283). F7 and fixture-derived. Removing the scatter filter in memory failed the scatter test. |\n    22\t| 16 · Repeated series cues | Major | **Fixed with a new defect** | Compact bars now have 32 colour/pattern combinations. Scatter’s 64 combinations satisfy amended F9. The compact bar change also makes some previously distinct patterns identical. [scene/bars.ts:11](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:11), [view/index.ts:73](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:73) | [“spec F9: at least 32 distinct combinations…” → “bar (compact: true)”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/scene/scene.test.ts:702). F9-derived count. **None** checks the lost non-colour distinction. |\n    23\t\n    24\t## New defects\n    25\t\n    26\t1. **Blocker · A typed append can return the wrong source row.** Start a line with typed x `[0,1]`, y `[0,10]`, and `missing: 'zero'`. Append `[{x:2,y:20},{x:3,y:null},{x:4,y:40}]`. Hovering x=2 reports index 0 and `{x:0,y:0}`. When the null forces an explicit index, initialize the identity entries through the slots already written in that batch. [store-buffers.ts:109](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:109), [store.ts:824](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:824)\n    27\t\n    28\t2. **Blocker · A hidden, paused chart still retains unbounded history.** Draw x=2 with `keep:1`, Pause, hide the container, then append x=3 through 503 with `keep:1` and let each frame run. The store retains **502 rows**. Normalize the absent displayed frame to `null` before comparing it with the next frame, and keep the baseline stable while unmeasured. [controller.ts:1495](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1495), [controller.ts:1504](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1504)\n    29\t\n    30\t3. **Blocker · Tick formatter re-entry can starve publication.** Install a tick formatter that calls `update({title:'New title'})` each time. The old title was still visible after six frames, with another frame pending. Key prepared ticks on axis inputs so a title-only update can reuse them. A formatter that instead switches to an unformatted field and throws also delivers a stale AX160 under the new title. Check the frame generation before publishing those findings. [axes.ts:87](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:87), [controller.ts:1250](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1250)\n    31\t\n    32\t4. **Major · Paused re-encoding loses held findings and raw row information.** Hold a ninth series, change y to another populated field, then call `update({strict:true})`. AX130 disappears and strict succeeds until Resume. In scatter, a displayed row with old `x:null` and valid alternate `u` appears only after Resume when switching x to `u`. Re-encoding a typed `NaN` while paused can also raise a false omission note. Validate both views before accepting either and re-encode the displayed raw window with its typed-column provenance. [controller.ts:605](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:605), [controller.ts:642](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:642), [controller.ts:740](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:740)\n    33\t\n    34\t5. **Major · A frozen scatter frame changes month precision.** Queue a March `YYYY-MM` point with `keep:1`, Pause before its frame, then append April through December with `keep:1` before drawing. March reads **“Mar 1, 2026”** even though hover still returns the original `{x:'2026-03',y:3}`. Read date precision through the same owned-row accessor as hover. [controller.ts:311](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:311), [controller.ts:1834](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1834)\n    35\t\n    36\t6. **Major · A throwing getter bypasses strict and can undo teardown.** On a valid strict line, append a row whose x getter throws. The call returns and the chart shows AX199. A nested `update` from a getter also clears the outer strict context. A getter that calls `destroy()` and returns lets the outer update repopulate the destroyed handle’s diagnostics. Keep preparation state local to each call, use it for append, and check liveness before acceptance. [controller.ts:495](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:495), [controller.ts:530](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:530), [controller.ts:662](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:662)\n    37\t\n    38\t7. **Major · Scatter still does data-sized work on a pointer move.** The first hover at the centre of a 32,000-point ring builds the lattice even though the counter reports only 2,679 visits. With 50,000 points sharing x and a hover subscriber, picking row 49,999 read **50,001 row indexes** during payload construction. Build the fallback with the lookup and reuse the point index already located by the pick. [scatter-grid.ts:325](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:325), [scatter.ts:30](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter.ts:30), [controller.ts:1603](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1603)\n    39\t\n    40\t8. **Major · Lattice tooltip paging can repeat page one.** Pin the centre pick of that ring at DPR 1. The lookup counts 14 points and provides eight. The pager reconstructs only those eight from raw anchors, so `+6 more` returns the same rows. Page from the winning grid group using the same membership rule that produced the count. [focus.ts:171](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:171), [interaction.ts:662](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:662)\n    41\t\n    42\t9. **Major · An estimated strip can blank a readable chart.** Give a donut 112 px of plot room. With the recording host using the CSS strip’s 48 px minimum, the controller estimates 30 px, reserves the strip, then shows AX142 and no marks at 64 px. Use the strip’s own line height or retry without the strip before entering L8. [controller.ts:1315](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1315), [controller.ts:1353](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1353), [css.ts:190](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:190)\n    43\t\n    44\t10. **Major · Narrow scatter still drops the automatic x endpoint.** Draw x `1.1, 8.9, 10.7` with the last y null, then resize the recording host to 185 × 400. The plot remains readable with x domain `[0,12]` and ticks `[0,5,10]`. Use the same extent for domain and tick selection, and apply the coarser-domain fitting path to scatter x. [axes.ts:137](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:137), [layout/index.ts:251](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/layout/index.ts:251)\n    45\t\n    46\t11. **Major · Watcher acquisition can get stuck on reattachment.** Detach and reattach a chart, with the environment watcher throwing once after the theme watcher starts. The observer path leaves `watching` set and subsequent resize notifications skip setup. Roll back that invocation’s subscriptions and reset `watching` on failure. This is source-traced. [chart.ts:101](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:101), [chart.ts:148](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:148)\n    47\t\n    48\t12. **Major · Memory accounting omits live buffers.** Draw 1,001 streamed line rows, Pause, then append with `keep:2`. The benchmark reported 8,714 B while the displayed frame alone still held 23,625 B in omitted column buffers. At store level, preparing a competing tail fill and then reading the old frame also creates a cached copy that `ownedBytes()` skips. Count buffers from every live frame with one deduplication set, including already-materialized getter copies. [instrument.ts:149](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/instrument.ts:149), [store-bytes.ts:58](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-bytes.ts:58), [store-buffers.ts:269](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:269)\n    49\t\n    50\t13. **Major · Compact bar patterns lose an A5 distinction.** Draw three equal-height series in one compact category. Series indexes 1 and 2 now both use diagonal fill and differ only in colour. Preserve a distinguishable non-colour cue across the palette while keeping the 32 F9 combinations. Adding pattern types would require extending `RectMark.pattern` and both renderers. [scene/bars.ts:18](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:18), [contracts.ts:469](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:469)\n    51\t\n    52\t14. **Minor · Scatter retains a duplicate x column after the last missing point is evicted.** Append a null-y row and a valid row, then append another valid row with `keep:2`. `missingX` is gone but `ownedBytes()` still lists `x positions`. Drop that column when every retained row is again represented by the point x column. [store-unaligned.ts:157](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-unaligned.ts:157), [store-unaligned.ts:187](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-unaligned.ts:187)\n    53\t\n    54\t## Claims not confirmed\n    55\t\n    56\t- The test named “the frame draws 3” actually leaves `[0,1,2]` on screen for that frame, then draws `[4]`. Removing the in-flight pin in memory left all 37 final-review tests green. A focused commit-time eviction probe changed from the correct row to `row:null` with that removal. I also observed a throwing value formatter run again after the first figure write in the Node host. [final-review.test.ts:25](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:25), [controller.ts:1188](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1188)\n    57\t- The wider snapshot properties compare frame contents and captions. They do not independently check the zoomed marks, skip collapsed and faulted frames, and never exercise scatter hover provenance. The path assertion is an upper bound, and the retention assertion allows eleven extra rows. [final-review.test.ts:442](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:442), [final-review.test.ts:639](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:639)\n    58\t- The shared-tree reports do not establish browser results, I1/P4 latency, lifetime heap behaviour or packed byte counts for `bbd7564`. The candidate and byte-count tests cover narrower measurements. [scatter.test.ts:516](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/lookup/scatter.test.ts:516), [streaming-storage.test.ts:133](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts:133)\n    59\t\n    60\t**This part is not ready for the release acceptance run.** The blockers are the DX7 packed-size gate, defects 1–13 above, and missing focused regressions for in-flight ownership, held-datum eviction and reattachment cleanup and font measurement. The deliberate P7 failure and the redundant scatter x column are outside that blocker list.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show HEAD:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/fixes-verify.interaction.review.md | nl -ba'","aggregated_output":"     1\t<!-- Reviewer: Codex, requested gpt-6.2-astra xhigh; observed model gpt-6.2-astra, effort xhigh (session rollout turn_context, thread from the events file). Read-only, cross-provider review of commit bbd7564. Saved by the coordinator. -->\n     2\t\n     3\t**No. At `bbd7564`, the original held-mouse-click and empty-window-reset blockers are fixed. A pin can still switch to a different series, a redraw can strand a pressed row, and a focused category can be announced again solely because its ordinal changed.**\n     4\t\n     5\tI read the committed blobs with `git show bbd7564:<path>`. I ran six committed Node suites in memory using Node’s test runner, Vitest assertions, and fast-check. No files changed. Browser behavior below is a source trace unless identified as a Node result.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Findings from the final review\n     8\t\n     9\tSeverity is the original review’s **B** blocker, **M** major, or **m** minor. Source filenames are under `packages/axylo/src`. Browser test names below give the file stem, line, and identifying part of the test title. A named test covers the stated case. **None** identifies a missing regression test.\n    10\t\n    11\t| Finding | Severity | Status | Evidence at `bbd7564` | Reverting test |\n    12\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n    13\t| 1 · Held mouse click | B | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:1222,1232` picks the mouse-release coordinates independently of `held`. | `final-hold:43` “Q4’s exact datum and row”, `:61` “a click selects B”, `:93` “empty hole selects nothing” |\n    14\t| 2 · Empty-window reset | B | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:805,1748,1797` clears the state-text cache and establishes focus before writing or drawing. | `final-pin:26` “focus, reading, ring, tooltip and Enter agree on x 0” |\n    15\t| 3 · All-zero donut actions | B | **fixed with a new defect** | `interaction.ts:216,257,267` gives the list one stop and native activation. Replacing its entries can drop focus at `:264`. | `final-pin:53` “Tab reaches the slice list”; **none** for a focused list redraw |\n    16\t| 4 · Placement and clipping | B | **partly fixed** | `placement.ts:98,144,169` shifts around supplied obstacles and rejects oversize boxes. `interaction.ts:755,765` supplies incomplete clipping and focus obstacles. | `focus-placement:47,58,64,102` control shift, clipped alignment, overwidth, fallback; **none** for the omitted geometry below |\n    17\t| 5 · Hoverable route | B | **fixed with a new defect** | `interaction.ts:483,1084` and `placement.ts:209` give all placements the same rested route. A stationary pointer does not start a new rest when a commit changes its datum at `interaction.ts:1778`. | `final-hold:119,139,156,172` dense edge, horizontal strip, scatter strip, no-rest converse; **none** for rest interrupted by a frame |\n    18\t| 6 · Accessible and selectable pin rows | M | **partly fixed** | `tooltip.ts:125,198,220` exposes named buttons and paging. `focus.ts:171` can omit actual group members. `tooltip.ts:356` can leave the only row or paging button clipped. | `final-pin:115` named AX buttons, `:153` ten exact coincidences, `:182` secondary strip tap; **none** for interrupted group order or a clipped last action |\n    19\t| 7 · Press across redraw | M | **partly fixed** | `tooltip.ts:153` reuses a row in the same presentation. Its aligned key includes formatted text at `:75`. Switching presentation discards the node at `:248,257`. | `final-pin:133` “secondary row held across an append”; **none** for reordering, reformatting, or crossing the strip threshold during a press |\n    20\t| 8 · Hold outlives geometry | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:1770,1803` re-picks after ordinary geometry changes. `:319` ignores sub-half-pixel changes, and `:1829` drops a held presentation without clearing its rest. | `final-hold:187` “Q4 at once, without a move”; `:206` only excludes Q3 after resize |\n    21\t| 9 · Pin and dismissal identity | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:1688` checks the original scatter ref. Escape uses the group’s current first ref at `:1365`, and `pointer.ts:41` searches only the capped sample. Aligned pins replace their ref at `interaction.ts:1698`. | `final-pin:222,241` hide pinned A and dismiss A before adding B; **none** for reversed operation order, sample overflow, or hidden aligned A |\n    22\t| 10 · Wrong focus geometry | M | **fixed** for the reported datum ring and single-series union | `interaction.ts:691,745,762` independently supplies the keyboard ring and the union of displayed marks. `focus.ts:344,370` uses the same ring geometry for painting and exclusion. | `final-pin:258` “covers neither series’ point”; `focus-placement:73` “keyboard ring elsewhere”. **None** for omitting that ring at the DOM call site while hovering B. |\n    23\t| 11 · Donut hole | M | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:750` supplies both scaled radii after clearance. `placement.ts:131` tests the farthest corners and the ring strokes before the other candidates. | `focus-placement:121,127,133` oversized tip, fitting tip in an enclosing slice box, crossing stroke |\n    24\t| 12 · Short plots | M | **partly fixed** | `controller.ts:1323` selects three modes, and `css.ts:192` reserves two strip line heights. The initial eligibility calculation still uses the plot text’s estimated height at `controller.ts:1316`. | `final-review.test.ts:255,265` “92 px plot” and “keeps 80 px”; `final-hold:380` “never a floating tooltip”. **None** for an actual strip height different from the estimate. |\n    25\t| 13 · Transformed ancestors | M | **partly fixed** | `mapping.ts:47,65,69` uses fractional, independent scales. `chart.ts:196` retains the **known** measurement issue. The promised transform limit is absent from spec §3.8 at `02-product-spec.m