{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_119","type":"agent_message","text":"**Hold release acceptance.** Three original blockers remain open, and the changes introduced two more.\n\nReviewed HEAD `f5cc8b3`. Its source, tests, and review rules match `e90d8db`, the HEAD at the start of the review. I ran the targeted Node suites and read-only probes against HEAD and `bbd7564`. Browser test coverage and DOM behavior were assessed from source. No files were changed.\n\n```text\nTest Files  21 passed (21)\n     Tests  467 passed (467)\n```\n\n## Table 1. Verification defects\n\n`C` identifies the controller review’s numbered findings. `I` identifies the interaction review’s rows in order. The test column names the assertions that would catch a revert and identifies their basis.\n\n| Defect | Severity | Status | Evidence at HEAD | Reverting test and basis |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| C1 · Typed append returns the wrong row | Blocker | **Fixed** | Materializing the index now fills identity entries through the slots already written in the batch. [store-buffers.ts:109](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:109) | “The reviewer’s sequence: x [0, 1] … append 2, null at 3, 4.” Fixture rows and the source-index contract. [streaming-storage.test.ts:750](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts:750) |\n| C2 · Hidden, paused history grows without bound | Blocker | **Partly fixed** | Continuous hiding keeps the baseline stable. Showing the same paused frame again resets it to the growing store size. Alternating hide, append with `keep: 1`, and show retained **102 rows** while still displaying only x=2. [controller.ts:1611](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1611), [controller.ts:1620](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1620) | “x=2 drawn with keep 1, Pause, hide, 500 appends…” Fixture for the rows and implementation policy for `2 × baseline + 8`. **None** for repeated hide/show. [verify-pass.test.ts:28](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:28) |\n| C3 · Tick formatter re-entry stalls drawing or publishes stale AX160 | Blocker | **Fixed** | Title-only updates reuse prepared tick labels. The generation check runs before tick findings are published. [axes.ts:92](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:92), [controller.ts:1348](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1348) | “Switches to an unformatted field and throws” and “calls update({ title }) on every call.” DX5 and §3.5. [verify-pass.test.ts:56](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:56) |\n| I1 · Touch release and Enter activate the wrong datum | Blocker | **Fixed** | A tap uses its release coordinates. Enter and Space select the datum described by the focused range. [interaction.ts:1042](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1042), [interaction.ts:1354](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1354) | “A touch down 1 px inside A’s half…” and “Enter selects the datum the focused range describes.” Decision 0004 and fixture coordinates. [final-verify.browser.test.ts:26](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:26) |\n| I2 · Pin follows another datum | Blocker | **Fixed** | Reconciliation retains the saved ref and ends the pin if that ref leaves or is hidden. The same check runs after Resume. [interaction.ts:1897](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1897) | “Pin aligned A … hide A … the pin ends.” Rule 8. **None** specific to a narrowed secondary ref surviving a redraw or Resume. [final-verify.browser.test.ts:61](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:61) |\n| I3 · Invisible pin traps interaction | Blocker | **Fixed** | Drag and pinch start end the pin. Failed placement also ends it and presents the current pick. [interaction.ts:816](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:816), [interaction.ts:1248](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1248), [interaction.ts:1487](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1487) | “Pin a point, start a drag, Escape…” Rules 4 and 7 and the gesture clarification. **None** for pinch without a committed zoom. [final-verify.browser.test.ts:82](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:82) |\n| I4 · Clipped rows pass the fit test | Blocker | **Partly fixed** | Floating fit checks intrinsic overflow, and a wholly clipped strip is hidden. A strip still passes when one row overflows or when only a sliver of it intersects the visible region. A long title can still hide the row and pager. [tooltip.ts:378](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:378), [tooltip.ts:430](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:430) | “A strip its card clips away entirely…” and the conditional “chart clipped to a short visible band” check. Rules 5–6 and measured geometry. **None** for a long title crowding out the first row or pager. [final-verify.browser.test.ts:112](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:112), [final-verify.browser.test.ts:146](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:146) |\n| I5 · Wrong visible region or covered chart control | Blocker | **Partly fixed** | Placement intersects the plot and tooltip clipping chains and crosses shadow hosts. The walk skips `assignedSlot`, so a clipping wrapper around a slot is missed. Chart controls get a fixed 3 viewport px allowance even when a transform enlarges the outline. Rule 2 covers the chart’s own controls. [mapping.ts:90](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/mapping.ts:90), [interaction.ts:846](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:846) | “A chart in a shadow root inside a clipping card…” Rules 2 and 10. Its geometry assertions are conditional on a tip appearing. **None** for slots or a scaled control outline. [final-verify.browser.test.ts:170](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:170) |\n| C4 · Paused re-encoding loses findings or raw rows | Major | **Partly fixed** | The reported AX130, null-x and typed-NaN cases are covered. The displayed window’s option findings are discarded, so strict accepts a field available only in held rows and blanks the plot. The backward scan also misses a retained imputed-zero row behind an evicted source index. [controller.ts:645](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:645), [controller.ts:842](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:842) | “A ninth series held,” “a displayed row with x null,” and “a NaN in a typed column.” §3.5, F2, I6 and fixtures. **None** for displayed-only AX101 or sparse source indexes. [verify-pass.test.ts:95](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:95) |\n| C5 · Frozen scatter loses month precision | Major | **Fixed** | Date precision reads through the owned-row accessor used for event payloads. [controller.ts:1126](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1126), [controller.ts:1952](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1952) | “March (YYYY-MM) queued with keep 1…” F4 and fixture. The assertion checks the year and absence of a day number. [verify-pass.test.ts:145](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:145) |\n| C6 · Throwing or re-entrant getter bypasses strict or teardown | Major | **Partly fixed** | The three reported row-getter paths are covered by per-call preparation and liveness checks. A throwing option getter still runs in `preview()` before strict is set. A strict chart then accepts AX199 and shows the error state. [controller.ts:565](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:565), [controller.ts:595](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:595), [controller.ts:717](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:717) | “Strict: an append whose x getter throws,” “a getter that runs a nested update,” and “a getter that destroys the chart.” DX5 and §3.5. **None** for a throwing option getter. [verify-pass.test.ts:164](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:164) |\n| C7 · Scatter does data-sized work on pointer move | Major | **Partly fixed** | The fallback lattice is built with the lookup for the reported ring. Payload construction still walks equal-y or unrecognized-y runs. A hover on the latest of 50,000 coincident points read **50,000 row indexes**. [scatter-grid.ts:348](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:348), [controller.ts:1982](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1982) | “The first pick at the centre of a 32,000-point ring” and “50,000 points at one x.” The work caps are test-selected. The latter fixture uses distinct numeric y values and takes its expected y from the normalized column. **None** for coincident payload cost. [scatter.test.ts:631](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/lookup/scatter.test.ts:631), [verify-pass.test.ts:223](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:223) |\n| C8 · Lattice paging repeats page one | Major | **Fixed with a new defect** | The reported ring now has a second page, but it contains six rows outside the winning lattice group. See R3. [focus.ts:174](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:174), [interaction.ts:739](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:739